        "math_academy_id": "q-72001",
        "problem": "Evaluate the double integral ${\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x,\\, & \\text{if}\\,-2<x<0,\\,1<y<3, \\\\ \\frac{x}{y},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<2,\\,1<y<3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(-2,0)\\times (1,3)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,2)\\times (1,3).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}\\frac{1}{2}x\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}\\frac{x}{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\u222c}_{{R}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{{R}_{2}}(x)(\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3-1){\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}y+({\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]_{-2}^{0}+[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]_{0}^{2}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|y|]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(0-2)+(2-0)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1)) \\\\  & =-2+2(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)-0) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
